---
alwaysApply: true
---

Write confident, production-ready code.

- Avoid unnecessary defensive or tentative code.
- Do not add redundant null/undefined checks when values are already validated by the caller, schema, or middleware.
- Do not use unnecessary optional chaining (`?.`) or nullish coalescing (`??`) unless they handle a real edge case.
- Assume function contracts are respected unless the requirement states otherwise.
- Keep the code simple, deterministic, and readable.
- Validate inputs only at the API/service boundary, not repeatedly throughout the call stack.
- Every conditional, fallback, or guard clause must have a clear functional reason.
